{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetKC1Gs3WWAMjhpTPtMS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-14` — Shipment data class with shipmentId, orderId, carrier, and status\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:15-26` — save(), existsById(), findById() methods\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:26-56` — POST /shipments (create), GET /{shipmentId}, GET (list)\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:19-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n\n**Conventions:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses, not returning error responses\n2. ConflictException for HTTP 409, ResourceNotFoundException for 404\n3. Both exceptions take ErrorCode enum and a message string\n4. Tests use MockMvc with `post()` / `get()`, `status().isCreated` / `.isConflict` / `.isNotFound`, and `jsonPath()` assertions\n5. Response envelopes use `$.error.code` path for error codes\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Add ErrorCode for shipment state conflict (e.g., `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED`)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add 4 new tests covering the confirm scenarios\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding ErrorCode changes the enum which is part of the public API; must ensure it's semantically correct\n- Confirm endpoint logic must handle all three cases (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- Must not break existing tests\n\n**Open questions:** None — requirement specifies all cases clearly.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to the ErrorCode enum to represent the conflict when confirming a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that:\n   - Finds the shipment by ID; throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If status is CREATED, updates to CONFIRMED, saves, and returns it\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, returns it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four new test methods:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment → transitions to CONFIRMED and persists\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment → returns unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment → returns 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment → returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Instead of adding a new ErrorCode, reuse `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` for the CANCELLED case — rejected because ALREADY_EXISTS semantically means the shipment exists as created earlier (conflict on creation), not that it's in an invalid state. A separate code better communicates the domain constraint.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED shipment | repository.findById(id) returns CREATED | repository.save(shipment.copy(status=CONFIRMED)) | 200 OK + Shipment JSON | Return ResponseEntity.ok(saved) |\n| CONFIRMED shipment | repository.findById(id) returns CONFIRMED | None | 200 OK + unchanged Shipment JSON | Return ResponseEntity.ok(foundShipment) |\n| CANCELLED shipment | repository.findById(id) returns CANCELLED | None | 409 Conflict + error envelope | Throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED, message) |\n| Unknown shipment | repository.findById(id) returns null | None | 404 Not Found + error envelope | Throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message) |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. `confirmCreatedShipmentTransitionsToConfirmed()` — Create shipment, confirm it, assert status is now CONFIRMED and response has 200 status\n2. `confirmAlreadyConfirmedShipmentIdempotent()` — Create, confirm once, confirm again, assert 200 and status unchanged (idempotent)\n3. `confirmCancelledShipmentReturnsConflict()` — Create a CANCELLED shipment directly in repository, attempt confirm, assert 409 and code is SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED\n4. `confirmUnknownShipmentReturnsNotFound()` — Attempt confirm on non-existent ID, assert 404 and code is SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nFirst, I'll add the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":909,"cache_read_input_tokens":18947,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":909},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c307104-e57c-412b-8edf-03d36ac9d483","uuid":"d76153b1-6209-4912-bab3-cfd48cc88542","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:10:01.382Z","request_id":"req_011CetKBzeQxt2nf8Tv33EtL"}
